# JARVIS Product Requirements Document

## Governance note

This document is the product governance baseline for JARVIS. It is intentionally split into status categories so that current, locked, proposed, and future scope remain distinct.

- LOCKED: invariants that are non-negotiable and already reflected in repo guidance.
- CURRENT: verified scope already represented in the project history and implementation state.
- PROPOSED: planned work that is in design or backlog and not yet proven in source.
- FUTURE: out-of-scope or intentionally deferred capabilities that must not be claimed as implemented.

## LOCKED

- JARVIS is a modular, mobile-first AI business operating system for founders, operators, and small businesses.
- Security and least privilege are authoritative.
- AI is functionality, not decoration.
- Backend authorization is authoritative; frontend never accesses the database directly.
- Default deny, least privilege, and fail-closed policy apply.
- High and critical actions require approval unless an explicit policy permits otherwise.
- Unknown risk is treated as Critical.
- LOCK ALL blocks side effects and fails closed.
- No fabricated data; read-oriented dashboard states remain distinct: LOADING, EMPTY, UNAVAILABLE, ERROR, DATA.
- Provider SDKs remain behind adapters and are never treated as business logic.
- Android/Kotlin remains isolated; web implementation batches do not rewrite the Android app.

## CURRENT

### Users and use cases

| User | Primary use |
| --- | --- |
| Owner / founder | See business state, manage work, approve risk, configure policy |
| Admin | Administer authorized users and operational configuration |
| Operator | Execute permitted workflows within assigned scope |
| Viewer | Read permitted operational information |
| AI agent | Independent system actor with explicit identity, scope, permissions, and risk ceiling; never a human user |

### Core modules

- Core: Auth, Dashboard, Tasks, Clients, Agents, Approvals, Security, Audit.
- Operations: Communications, Content, Finance, Integrations.
- AI: Orchestrator, Memory, Tool Gateway, Voice, Agent Registry.

