## PROPOSED

### Planned MVP requirements

1. Authentication foundation and session boundaries.
2. Read-oriented dashboard.
3. Security Center with security state and emergency LOCK ALL controls.
4. Roles, permissions, resource scopes, and agent risk ceilings.
5. Approval Center for consequential actions.
6. Append-only Audit Log.
7. Agent Registry for the planned agents.
8. Task and Client foundations.
9. Integration inventory and Finance visibility foundations.
10. AI usage visibility and configuration foundations.
11. Responsive mobile-first UI with polished desktop behavior.
12. Source-of-truth documentation and AI coding guidance.

### Planned agent registry

The planned registry contains CEO/Orchestrator, Business, Client, Developer, QA, Sales, Finance, Email, Content, Creator Revenue, Portfolio, Security, and Analytics. Registry presence is not proof of execution.

### Planned roadmap themes

- Dashboard polish and state fidelity.
- Informational and operational modules.
- Hardening, verification, and production boundaries.
- Production auth and DB integration.
- Authorized external integrations.
- Provider-backed AI execution with tool allowlists and approval.
- Scheduler and multi-agent workflow coordination.

## FUTURE

The following are future or explicitly deferred items and must not be claimed as implemented:

- Real provider-backed AI execution.
- Real OAuth or credential-based integration flows.
- Production authentication and session management.
- Production database integration and migration execution.
- Scheduler-driven autonomous jobs.
- Multi-agent workflows with bounded delegation.
- Voice-first UX and conversation gateway.
- External finance execution such as bank login, UPI, ATM PIN, OTP handling, or payment transfers.

Unless verified in source, no real AI execution, payments, transfers, OAuth integrations, or voice features are implemented. Finance remains limited to verified visibility and planning data.

## Non-functional requirements

- Security and least privilege are authoritative.
- APIs are typed and observable.
- Sensitive actions are auditable and approval-gated.
- UI is accessible, responsive, and honest about data state.
- Documentation must remain source-of-truth and must not be used to infer feature completion.

